## mgs-mola-megdr-4ppd@2003-grid-pds4-label-1.1

- Provider: NASA PDS Geosciences Node, Washington University; MGS MOLA Team / David E. Smith.
- Bundle: https://pds-geosciences.wustl.edu/mgs/urn-nasa-pds-mgs_mola_topography_derived/ ; DOI 10.17189/1z1b-kv84.
- Products: data_meg004:megt90n000cb (topography), data_meg004:megc90n000cb (observation counts); PDS4 labels version 1.1, September 15 2026. Underlying grid is the final 2003 MEGDR, not new 2026 observations.
- Retrieved/processed: 2026-10-07. Stored grids and labels: crates/cosmogon_sim/data/mola/. Exact hashes and provider URLs: metadata.json.
- Rights evidence: Geosciences Node January 2024 FAQ, page 2, “Data sets archived in the PDS are in the public domain.” https://pds-geosciences.wustl.edu/documents/ViewingPDSImagesAndExportingToOtherFormats.pdf . Attribution retained; project licence does not replace source attribution.
- Raw source SHA256: topography 25f16fb7aaf857898dcf98bc4f841341a24f8b9f7e98453ca083bc45d897ca2c; counts 7e920ec43497b4beddf974650471600c7afd4916e2a8dd3500d6b14714365661. Both also matched the provider's archive MD5 inventory at retrieval.
- Spatial coordinates: IAU2000 planetocentric latitude, positive-east longitude; 1440 × 720, 0.25° centres from (89.875 N, 0.125 E), rows north to south. About 14.817845 km equatorial sampling on the source reference sphere.
- Vertical coordinates: signed integer metres, median topography (radius minus GMM3/mgm1025 degree/order 50 areoid radius). No height uncertainty/covariance supplied per bin.
- Observations: mapping phase February 1999 through June 2001, plus specified off-nadir polar observations in 1998/mapping. Labels' broader observation timestamps are retained in the XML.
- Processing: tools/process_mola.py validates pinned raw SHA256, dimensions, type and label version, then converts big-endian to little-endian without resampling. Runtime bilinear heights expose four source-cell medians, observation counts and weights; zero counts mark provider-interpolated bins. Counts are not confidence or uncertainty.
- Limits: global overview, not local geology, engineering/landing safety or a current terrain survey. No random subgrid elevation is added to Mars. Colours, climate, resource distribution and fine shading remain generated/modelled; the renderer uses a spherical base rather than the full areoid shape. Future grid revisions must receive a distinct saved terrain identifier to preserve old worlds.


## mars-landing-references@2026-10-07.1

- Provider: NASA Langley NTRS (Perseverance) and NASA GISS Mars24 (Curiosity, InSight, Viking 1).
- References: https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210024644 ; https://www.giss.nasa.gov/tools/mars24/help/landers.html . Read 2026-10-07; source acquisition/narrative dates 2021-11-19 / 2023-12-09.
- Imported fields: historical UTC landing date, north latitude, east longitude, stable ID and citation. Embedded factual transcription in crates/cosmogon_sim/src/planet/landing.rs; explicit reviewed updates only. No copied source narrative, imagery, tracks, mission status or new Universe fields.
- Rights: NTRS declares US Government public use permitted. GISS numerical reference facts are cited individually; no image rights are inferred and no mission media is copied.
- Uncertainty: unavailable/null. Complete source frame/datum/covariance is not established by these summaries. Overview interpretation uses the MOLA planetocentric body-fixed convention and existing simulated axial tilt/spin; not metre-level registered coordinates or a SPICE solution.
- Use: native historical landing markers, coordinate selection/camera travel, source-supported probe JSON and CLI sites/surface. No fabricated current rover positions or landing-safety claims.


## mgs-mola-megdr-16ppd@2003-grid-pds4-label-1.1

- Same NASA PDS/MGS MOLA provider, attribution, public-domain archive FAQ and DOI as the 4ppd field above. Retrieved/processed 2026-10-08. Numerical grids, primary labels and provider checksum inventory are retained in crates/cosmogon_sim/data/mola16/.
- Products: data_meg016:megt90n000eb and data_meg016:megc90n000eb; PDS4 labels version 1.1. Provider inventory URL: https://pds-geosciences.wustl.edu/mgs/urn-nasa-pds-mgs_mola_topography_derived/urn-nasa-pds-mgs_mola_topography_derived.md5 . Inventory SHA256 4468a26e18e382896cb3abd4cd69362f0bc76920ec64bf3645271e7be4ebe487; both binary and XML MD5 match it.
- Raw SHA256: topography d18d9b9ab8c5516d02e157dd2cde0f1d0d160c21940e953ba22391269a545e7b; counts 9a300c6cd9f5a282ae31299be228ea2e75993049e88c9f6ab69a84f4db5f01d7. Exact processed/label checksums and URLs in metadata.json.
- Grid: 5760 × 2880, 0.0625° centres from (89.96875 N, 0.03125 E); IAU2000 planetocentric, positive-east. Source reference sphere 3,396,000 m; equatorial spacing 3.7044613374 km. Heights above GMM3/mgm1025 degree/order 50 areoid, not the app mean-radius datum. Observations/label-correction epochs remain as above.
- Verified binary height range −8177..21171 m; counts 0..326, with 903558 zero-shot bins. Provider reports about 55% of equatorial bins contain at least one shot and profile gaps up to 12 km. Finer pixels do not establish finer independent measurements. Null uncertainty stays null; counts are not confidence.
- Processing: exact endian conversion, no resampling/no invented cells. tools/process_mola.py --ppd 16 validates pinned raw/label/inventory SHA256, provider MD5, dimensions/axis order/type/version and nonnegative counts before any output writes. Bounded range downloads verify exact offsets and size; runtime decodes four immutable source cells without a second heap grid.
- Use: explicit undoable source selection, shared terrain/climate/resource queries, probes/landing markers, camera altitude, version-pinned geographic viewpoints/terrain sections and research manifests. Existing worlds/defaults preserve 4ppd or procedural fields. Source changes invalidate meshes/bakes and incompatible tracking. No local slope, current rover-path or landing-safety model is claimed.
